    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66-a2">

                <pb facs="0142" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg94"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 220.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 13,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon the 12th instant I had the honor to
                    receive your Imperial Highnesse’s dispatch, informing me that the ports of
                    Ichang, Wuhu, Wên-Chow, and Pakhoi would be opened to foreign trade upon the 1st
                    of April next, and that a date for opening the six landing-places upon the
                    Yangtze River would be announced after suitable regulations had been agreed
                    upon.</p>
                <p>I have instructed the consuls of my government at the several ports to
                    communicate the contents of your Imperial Highnesse’s dispatch to our
                    people.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To His Imperial Highness <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince Kung</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
